  "title": "Ageing Lutyens’ Delhi bungalows push upkeep bill for Union Ministers’ residences to over ₹92 crore",
  "summary": "The government allocated over ₹92 crore to maintain the upkeep of Delhi’s Lutyens bungalows, with annual expenditure reaching Rs 92.35 crore in 2025-26, more than three times the 27.47 crore in 2014-15. This reflects a growing challenge in preserving these iconic structures amid rising costs and infrastructure challenges.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The government spent ₹547.68 crore on such works between 2014-15 and 2025-26 through the Central Public Works Department (CPWD).",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The annual upkeep bill for 2025-26 was the highest since 2014, with inflation and age-related wear and tear contributing to the increase.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "CPWD officials highlighted maintenance challenges like seepage, termite infestation, and ageing systems.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
